# Design System Playbook — required reading

Before implementing, refactoring, or auditing any UI in `src/`, you MUST read:

**`docs/design/PLAYBOOK.md`**

The playbook is the operational layer of the design system — the mandatory workflow, anti-patterns, and self-audit checklist for building UI in this repo. Each rule exists because something went wrong once. **Do not re-debate rules already in the playbook** — implement according to the playbook. The spec it points to (tokens, foundations, patterns, motion, states, voice) lives in the other `docs/design/` documents.

## What the playbook covers

1. **Component canonical sources** — when to use `<Button>` primary vs ghost vs destructive, when to use `<Modal>` vs `<Sheet>`, when `<Combobox>` vs `<MultiTagAutocomplete>`, etc.
2. **Token conventions** — `--border` vs `--border-strong`, `--text-on-accent` light vs dark, status enum tokens, layout magic numbers.
3. **Canonical patterns by scenario** — confirm modal destructive, autocomplete with tags, filter chips display, section card disabled-gated, field-as-attribute, toast neutral-undo.
4. **Anti-patterns explicit** — no `<select>` HTML native, no Portal+div modals, no hardcoded `text-white`, no hardcoded literals, no inventing variants without ADR.
5. **Mandatory workflow before implementing UI** — read playbook, consult the component inventory in `docs/design/components.md` before creating any component (reuse before create; the `src/test/component-inventory-guard.test.ts` guardia keeps that catalog in lockstep with `src/components/`), then demo HTML, component spec, ADRs, tokens.
6. **Self-audit checklist before closing** — TodoWrite, visual verification vs demo, comparative audit, validation, snippet-in-report.
7. **Cross-cutting handling during a session** — flag instead of silent fix.
8. **What to update when a module closes** — playbook, the relevant `docs/design/` topic doc, ADR.

## Related sources of truth

Permanent design system (`docs/design/`):

- `docs/design/README.md` — design-system index + file-selection guide.
- `docs/design/visual-foundations.md` — color, typography, spacing, radius, surfaces, gradients.
- `docs/design/tokens-css.md` — literal CSS-variable contract (mirror of `src/app/globals.css`).
- `docs/design/interface-patterns.md` — layout, shell, modals, forms, chips, responsive, a11y.
- `docs/design/motion.md` — motion system.
- `docs/design/states.md` — cross-cutting empty/loading/error states.
- `docs/design/ux-copy.md` — voice + tone library.
- `docs/design/components.md` — component map (what exists, when to use, canonical `src/` path).
- `docs/design/decisions/` — accepted ADRs (0001–0014).

This system was produced by a redesign subproject, kept only as historical context (not a source of rules or specs to follow). The authoritative sources are `docs/design/` and the code in `src/`. For the visual reference of a screen, use its per-FRD prototype (`docs/product/<prd>/<frd>/prototype/<slug>.html`).

## Reinforcing rules also `alwaysApply: true`

- `coding-standards.mdc` — base coding behavior.
- `english-code-only.mdc` — code in English, copy in i18n.
- `validation-checklist.mdc` — final validation commands.
- `theme-light-dark.mdc` — both themes are first-class.
- `modal-canonical-pattern.mdc` — Modal canonical component (this rule's sibling for Modal specifically).

## When this rule applies

- Any creation, refactor, or audit of UI components in `src/components/`.
- Any creation, refactor, or audit of pages in `src/app/`.
- Any audit of a screen against its per-FRD prototype (`docs/product/<prd>/<frd>/prototype/<slug>.html`).

## Skip if

- Pure data-layer / Prisma / server-action changes with zero UI touch.
- Pure documentation work in `docs/product/` (FRDs, etc.) without code consequences.
- Test infrastructure that does not render UI.

For everything else: read the playbook first.
